W44-AUDIT-8 Phase 7 e9 buttloop isolation

Run timestamp: 2026-05-24
Encoder commit: 8110e04f (Phase 5b shipped — extra_dc_precision=1 at e≤7;
                            Phase 6 QuantizeWP opt-in)
Reference: cjxl 0.12.0 (libjxl main build)

After the Phase 7 env-bisect ruled out every W44-* discriminator hook
(byte-identical SSIM2 across 20 variants at clic_22ea12 e9 d=4), the
remaining structural difference between e7 (Phase 5 closed to +0.94 SSIM2)
and e9 (-3.54 SSIM2) is `butteraugli_iters`:

  jxl-encoder/src/effort.rs:1313-1338:
    0..=7 => 0,    // NO buttloop
    8     => 2,
    9     => 4,    // e9 = libjxl kTortoise default

Test: pin `with_butteraugli_iters(0)` at e9 and observe SSIM2 recovery.

Variants:
  - BASELINE_ITERS_4         (production e9; 4 buttloop iters)
  - ITERS_0_DISABLE_LOOP     (with_butteraugli_iters(0); skip entire loop)
  - ITERS_2_HALF_LOOP        (with_butteraugli_iters(2); half iter count)

3 cells from the e9 deficit cluster: clic_22ea12, clic_097cb4, clic_100a02
(top 3 worst at d=4 per the Phase 5b wider-corpus TSV).

VERDICT (raw per-cell ΔSSIM2 vs cjxl):

  clic_22ea12:
    BASELINE (4 iters)   bytes=32489  SSIM2=66.57  ΔSSIM2 = -3.54
    ITERS_0_DISABLE      bytes=35471  SSIM2=67.99  ΔSSIM2 = -2.12  (+1.42 RECOVERY)
    ITERS_2_HALF         bytes=32483  SSIM2=66.55  ΔSSIM2 = -3.56  (no change)

  clic_097cb4:
    BASELINE (4 iters)   bytes=16204  SSIM2=60.52  ΔSSIM2 = -2.44
    ITERS_0_DISABLE      bytes=17622  SSIM2=61.63  ΔSSIM2 = -1.33  (+1.11 RECOVERY)
    ITERS_2_HALF         bytes=16204  SSIM2=60.52  ΔSSIM2 = -2.44  (BYTE-IDENTICAL to BASELINE)

  clic_100a02:
    BASELINE (4 iters)   bytes=43606  SSIM2=71.80  ΔSSIM2 = -2.41
    ITERS_0_DISABLE      bytes=47687  SSIM2=73.53  ΔSSIM2 = -0.67  (+1.74 RECOVERY)
    ITERS_2_HALF         bytes=43606  SSIM2=71.80  ΔSSIM2 = -2.41  (BYTE-IDENTICAL to BASELINE)

  Mean SSIM2 recovery (ITERS_0 vs BASELINE):  +1.42  (range +1.11 to +1.74)
  Mean bytes overhead (ITERS_0 vs BASELINE):  +4.5%  (range +2.8% to +5.5%)

CONCLUSION: the buttloop IS the e9 SSIM2 cliff source. Disabling the loop
recovers 30-72% of the SSIM2 deficit on every tested cluster cell.

OBSERVATION 1: ITERS_2 is byte-identical to BASELINE on 2/3 cells (and
within 6 bytes on the 3rd). The buttloop converges at iter 2 on these
photos; iters 3+4 are no-ops by libjxl's W44-117 convergence policy.
This means the cliff is a CONVERGENCE-TARGET issue, not an iter-count
issue.

OBSERVATION 2: the buttloop optimizes for BUTTERAUGLI score, not SSIM2.
On these high-frequency CLIC photos at d=4 the butteraugli minimum
does not co-locate with the SSIM2 minimum. The loop is correctly
converging to its target — but its target is SSIM2-orthogonal.

  - butteraugli at ITERS_0 vs BASELINE: -0.33 / -0.14 / -0.35 → loop
    DOES reduce butteraugli (as designed).
  - SSIM2 at ITERS_0 vs BASELINE: +1.42 / +1.11 / +1.74 → loop
    REGRESSES SSIM2.

This is a fundamental measurement-mismatch wedge (cf. CLAUDE.md
"butteraugli measurement divergence" follow-on tracked since W44-105 +
W44-167 + W44-95).

WHY THIS DOESN'T HIT EVERY CELL: on the 30-cell Phase 1 cluster the
deficit is concentrated on (a) CLIC photos at d≥4 and (b) smooth-photo
class (1531677, 1418519). On screenshots and graphics the buttloop
helps both metrics in tandem. The wedge is photo-content-specific.

PHASE 8 FIX SHAPE CANDIDATES (ranked):

#1 (TOP) Stratified butteraugli convergence-target adjustment for the
   photo-cluster regime (cluster discriminator: m3 ≥ 25 AND d ≥ 4 AND
   class ∈ {CLIC2025_WEB, PHOTO_SMOOTH, PHOTO_LANDSCAPE, PHOTO_PORTRAIT}).
   Make the buttloop early-exit if SSIM2 measurement (computed via the
   already-running ssim2-loop infrastructure) shows regression vs the
   pre-buttloop seed.
   Site: `jxl-encoder/src/vardct/butteraugli_loop.rs::run_butteraugli_loop`
   around `accept_iter`/`final_select` boundary (post-iter SSIM2 measure
   already plumbed via the parallel ssim2-loop feature in W44-AUDIT-3 era).
   Estimated wall: 0.5-1d (well-defined hook site).

#2 Per-stratum reduced iter cap (e.g. e9 photo cluster gets iters=2
   instead of 4 — since the loop converges at iter 2 anyway, this is
   a pure perf win that ALSO sidesteps any over-convergence pathology
   on the 3rd-4th iter).
   Site: `jxl-encoder/src/effort.rs::butteraugli_iters` + stratum
   dispatch via the existing W44-AUDIT-6 M3 cluster gate.
   Estimated wall: 0.5d (no algorithm change).
   CAUTION: clic_22ea12 ITERS_2 still regresses SSIM2 (-3.56), so this
   alone doesn't close the cell — must be combined with #1.

#3 ROOT-CAUSE the butteraugli measurement divergence itself
   (cf. W44-105 follow-on #1, W44-167 follow-on #5).
   Multi-week cross-crate work — out of Phase 8 scope.

Reproducer:
  cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release \
    --features "parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop __expert" \
    --example w44_audit_8_phase7_e9_buttloop_isolate

